some very serious accusations in the  sunday times they have an interview with  the conservative mp nusrat ghani in  which she says that when she was sacked  as a minister from the department for  transport in february 2020 she was told  by government whip that the reason she  was sacked was because  some people  were  uncomfortable with her muslim women  minister status and that there were  concerns that she wasn't loyal to the  party and didn't do enough to defend the  conservative party against allegations  of islamophobia so very very serious  accusations  and in a pretty rare intervention the  chief whip  the boss of the whips and the government  enforcers in westminster mark spencer  has tweeted um this evening you don't  usually hear from chief whip so it is  quite a rare thing  to say that he was the person that nus  ghani is referring to these are the  tweets that he sent out he said to  ensure other whips are not drawn into  this matter i'm identifying myself as  the person nuzrat ghani mp has made  claims about this evening these  accusations are completely false and i  consider them to be defamatory i have  never used those words attributed to me  it is disappointed that when this issue  was raised before miss ghani she  declined to refer the mata to the  conservative party for a formal  investigation now in that interview with  the sunday times nuzghani says that the  reason why she didn't bring this up  sooner was because at the time  she was told that she would be  ostracized by colleagues if she brought  it up and that her career and her  reputation would be destroyed we have  heard from other government ministers  really mps from across the political  spectrum the education secretary nadim  zahawi tweeted uh saying that there  needed to be a proper investigation  there was no place for racism or  islamophobia tom tugenhart a senior mp  and conservative committee chair also  said there should be an inquiry as has  the former chief which mark harper and  also the labour party calling for an  investigation as well william rag who of  course is meeting the police to discuss  intimidation and blackmail accusations  next week  also said that he was appalled  and that the party needed to do better  now nus ghani was  the first  female woman muslim minister to speak  from the dispatch box she was applauded  and cheered when that  happened she says though that this  experience has left her feeling  powerless so more serious accusations  landing at the government's door as we  move into what's likely to be quite a  difficult week for the prime minister
 

